Subject: [PATCH 10/12 RFC] dt-bindings: media: let the decoder take a DOS syscon

A decoder whose DOS aperture is shared cannot own the region: the encoder
needs the same window. Give the node an amlogic,dos phandle for that case,
and make the region list and its names follow the phandle's presence —
both regions when the driver maps the aperture, only the parser region
when the syscon is mapped for it.

---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
index 18c9488..62f8bf9 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/amlogic,gx-vdec.yaml
@@ -49,12 +49,16 @@ properties:
       - const: esparser
 
   reg:
-    minItems: 2
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 2
 
   reg-names:
-    items:
-      - const: dos
-      - const: esparser
+    oneOf:
+      - items:
+          - const: dos
+          - const: esparser
+      - items:
+          - const: esparser
 
   resets:
     maxItems: 1
@@ -86,6 +90,13 @@ properties:
     description: should point to a canvas provider node
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
 
+  amlogic,dos:
+    description: |
+      Should point to the DOS syscon when the aperture is shared with another
+      engine. The driver then accesses it through the syscon instead of
+      mapping the "dos" region, so the node carries only the "esparser" one.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+
   power-domains:
     description:
       Power domain owning the AO sleep and isolation bits of the decoder.
@@ -136,6 +147,25 @@ allOf:
         clock-names:
           minItems: 5
 
+  # A shared DOS aperture is described by a syscon, and the node then only
+  # carries the parser region. Without one the driver maps the aperture
+  # itself, so both regions are required.
+  - if:
+      required:
+        - amlogic,dos
+    then:
+      properties:
+        reg:
+          maxItems: 1
+        reg-names:
+          maxItems: 1
+    else:
+      properties:
+        reg:
+          minItems: 2
+        reg-names:
+          minItems: 2
+
   # Platforms without a power domain keep programming the AO registers, so the
   # AO sysctrl stays mandatory for them.
   - if:
